  "title": "Golden Baked Мashed Potatoes",
  "description": "While you can just simply reheat mashed potatoes, or make pancakes, my favorite way to serve leftover mashed potatoes is this Fluffy Baked Mashed Potatoes.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you find yourself with more left over potatoes than you can deal with, this recipe is for you!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21358,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1677916843430} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21358-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Golden Baked Мashed Potatoes</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7732.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tWhile you can just simply reheat mashed potatoes, or make pancakes, my favorite way to serve leftover mashed potatoes is this Fluffy Baked Mashed Potatoes.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>1,2 kg potatoes</li><li>90 g butter</li><li>100 ml heavy cream or milk ((warm))</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper (to taste)</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Peel the potatoes. Chop the potatoes into cubes. Place them in a medium pot. Add salt to the water and cook for 15-20 minutes. When they are fork tender, strain the potatoes.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7686.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Add butter and mash until smooth and creamy. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7689.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Next, pour the warm heavy cream or milk. Add salt and pepper to taste.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7690.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Coat a baking dish with butter. Transfer potatoes to the prepared dish. You can make some shapes on the top.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7692.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Preheat oven to 400 degrees F. Bake uncovered for about 15 minutes until the top is golden.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_7726.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Main Dish</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
